---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About PDF Fluid" description="PDF Fluid explains how PDF files work and how to fix common PDF problems, in plain English.">
  <section class="page-head"><div class="container"><h1>About PDF Fluid</h1><p>Plain-English answers to every PDF problem.</p></div></section>
  <div class="container prose" style="max-width:760px;padding-top:24px;padding-bottom:56px">
    <p>PDF is the most widely used document format in the world, yet most people only notice it when something goes wrong: the file is too big to email, the text won't copy, the form won't save, or the password is lost.</p>
    <p><strong>PDF Fluid</strong> exists to fix that. Every guide starts with a short, direct answer, then explains <em>why</em> the problem happens and walks through solutions for Windows, Mac, phones and the browser — favouring free and built-in tools first.</p>
    <h2>Our principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Answer first.</strong> No long intros. The fix is at the top.</li>
      <li><strong>Explain the cause.</strong> Understanding how PDFs work helps you avoid the problem next time.</li>
      <li><strong>Free and built-in first.</strong> Most PDF tasks don't need paid software.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy-minded.</strong> We flag when an online tool uploads your file, and suggest local alternatives for sensitive documents.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Coming soon</h2>
    <p>We're building free PDF tools that run entirely in your browser, so your files never leave your device.</p>
    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Found a mistake, have a PDF problem we haven't covered, or want to suggest a tool? Email us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We read every message.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
